16. Definition of success

The research succeeds when an independent reviewer can:

- Reconstruct the specified object identifier from canonical bytes.
- Verify object and child-reference integrity.
- Detect invalid, missing, altered, and incomplete data.
- Understand the limits of a root digest.
- Distinguish object identity from object location, authorship, trust, freshness, and authorization.
- Confirm that object identity is independent of transport choice.
- Reproduce the regression results.
- Identify every unresolved protocol decision without relying on unstated assumptions.

17. Status and approval boundary

